1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,921
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:43,961
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,880
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:48,966
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,304
We got a report of a body. Rosebud Hotel.

7
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:55,889
PREVIOUSLY

8
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:57,933
It looks like she's been dead for a while.

9
00:00:58,016 --> 00:00:59,768
[Dr. Yoon] It's been at least 12 hours.

10
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:03,105
She was stabbed in three places,
but there's not much bleeding.

11
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:04,940
Do you know the victim?

12
00:01:05,524 --> 00:01:07,359
Her name's Oh Minyeong. She's a concierge.

13
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:09,611
Men just wouldn't leave her alone.

14
00:01:09,695 --> 00:01:11,321
She's gorgeous.

15
00:01:11,405 --> 00:01:13,532
Have you seen anyone suspicious lately?

16
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,492
Ah! Room 701.

17
00:01:15,576 --> 00:01:17,786
There's a suspect
in the seventh-floor suite.

18
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:19,288
[housekeeper] I heard he's a chaebol heir.

19
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:21,582
He kept calling for Minyeong,

20
00:01:21,665 --> 00:01:23,083
saying he had requests to make.

21
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:25,335
-Chunsik?
-Isoo!

22
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:26,837
You've been here three weeks.

23
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,131
-Did you run away from home?
-No, I just...

24
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:31,508
Is it because of Ms. Oh Minyeong?

25
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:35,387
[Chunsik] The person
I fell for at first sight is...

26
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:39,433
It's you, Minyeong.

27
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:41,435
Minyeong.

28
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:43,937
I'm sorry. I have a boyfriend.

29
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,025
Minyeong...

30
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:52,195
Do you know anyone who might've had
a grudge against Ms. Oh Minyeong?

31
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:54,448
[Seran] I saw everything, you bitch!

32
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:56,742
You've got it all wrong. It's not me!

33
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:58,785
You psycho bitch!

34
00:01:58,869 --> 00:02:02,247
Do you have any idea
who you're dealing with? Huh?

35
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:04,750
-Who was she?
-It was the hotel owner's wife.

36
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:08,045
The owner was dating Ms. Oh Minyeong?

37
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:11,173
There were rumors
that he was in love with her.

38
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:12,633
I have nothing else to say.

39
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:14,468
I said we're not done.

40
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:15,552
Let go.

41
00:02:16,094 --> 00:02:17,429
[soft thud]

42
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:19,556
He tried to drag her into Room 709?

43
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,975
That room has been vacant for two months.

44
00:02:22,601 --> 00:02:25,437
I kept that room for my own personal use.

45
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:29,232
We took the carpet in for testing,
and there wasn't enough blood.

46
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:31,526
I don't think she was murdered here.

47
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,528
She died somewhere else?

48
00:02:36,198 --> 00:02:37,449
[♪ foreboding music playing]

49
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:43,622
What's this?

50
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,291
[sniffs]

51
00:02:47,376 --> 00:02:49,044
[♪ music increases in tempo]

52
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:53,632
Are you checking out?

53
00:03:01,932 --> 00:03:03,141
[♪ music fades]

54
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:06,687
[Ms. Delta] Detective Jin, it's Room 701.
I came in to clean,

55
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:08,939
and I found something
that looks like blood.

56
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:10,232
What?

57
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,901
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

58
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:14,194
Kang Chunsik.

59
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:15,862
[♪ music increases in tempo]

60
00:03:20,117 --> 00:03:21,368
[swears softly]

61
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:23,578
[engine roaring, tires screech]

62
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,633
[Hyera exclaims] Watch out!

63
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:39,261
Don't worry. My car's more expensive.

64
00:03:40,512 --> 00:03:43,181
[scoffs] How dare he try to take me on?

65
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:45,642
[grunts softly]

66
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:47,477
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

67
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:48,979
-[siren blaring]
-[Isoo exclaims smugly]

68
00:03:56,695 --> 00:03:58,113
[tires screech, engine revs]

69
00:03:59,698 --> 00:04:01,032
[engine roaring]

70
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,627
Hey, hey.

71
00:04:12,711 --> 00:04:14,629
Vehicle ahead, stop the car.

72
00:04:15,297 --> 00:04:17,716
The trust-fund kid in car 6383!

73
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:19,301
Stop the car!

74
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,887
What's he doing?

75
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,556
[groans anxiously]

76
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,266
[Isoo, over loudspeaker] Stop the car!

77
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:29,561
[tires screeching]

78
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:34,608
[siren continues blaring]

79
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:37,861
My good citizens!

80
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:40,572
Chunsik Food's sole heir is on the run!

81
00:04:40,655 --> 00:04:43,074
We are police.

82
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:45,786
Kang Chunsik is on the run!

83
00:04:46,495 --> 00:04:48,371
Kang Chunsik, stop the damn car!

84
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:49,581
[sighs defeatedly]

85
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:51,792
[tires screeching]

86
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,168
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

87
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:56,004
That brat just won't listen.

88
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:58,173
Here we go.

89
00:04:58,256 --> 00:04:59,674
-[engine revs]
-[tires screeching]

90
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,761
[tires screech]

91
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:17,901
[tires screeching]

92
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:33,750
[tires screeching]

93
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,462
[siren continues blaring]

94
00:05:37,546 --> 00:05:38,547
[seat belt unbuckles]

95
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:40,006
[Hyera sighs]

96
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:42,384
[siren stops]

97
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:45,095
-What the hell are you doing?
-Mr. Kang Chunsik.

98
00:05:45,762 --> 00:05:47,806
You're under arrest
for the murder of Oh Minyeong.

99
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:49,099
-[handcuffs clicking]
-What?

100
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,187
Isoo. Why are you doing this to me?

101
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:56,439
What do you mean?
You just ran from the police.

102
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:58,275
We're taking you into custody, punk.

103
00:05:58,358 --> 00:05:59,359
[sputters]

104
00:06:00,110 --> 00:06:01,111
[snarls]

105
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:03,029
[Chunsik sputters]

106
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:05,574
Isoo!

107
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:07,367
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

108
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,376
EPISODE 6

109
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:32,225
[♪ music increases in tempo]

110
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:39,566
What kind of steak knife
comes with room service?

111
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:42,485
[♪ music fades]

112
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:43,570
Why did you run away?

113
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:47,365
I was just on my way home.

114
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:49,451
My car's just really fast.

115
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:53,121
You said Ms. Oh Minyeong
left your room around 7:40 p.m.

116
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:54,789
That's right.

117
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:56,124
What did you do after that?

118
00:06:56,207 --> 00:06:58,376
Oh, for god's sake.

119
00:06:58,460 --> 00:06:59,878
Answer the question.

120
00:07:02,547 --> 00:07:04,966
I was drinking because I was upset.

121
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:07,510
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

122
00:07:09,012 --> 00:07:10,096
[sniffles]

123
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:12,223
[crying softly]

124
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,356
[sniffles, sobbing]

125
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,109
And then?

126
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:28,365
[Chunsik] I ran out of alcohol,
so I went to the bar.

127
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:29,574
[sniffles]

128
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:38,667
Evening, sir.

129
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,047
-The usual, please.
-Yes, sir.

130
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,802
I was there until around 10:00 p.m.

131
00:07:51,638 --> 00:07:53,139
-[sighs softly]
-[cell phone vibrating]

132
00:07:58,269 --> 00:07:59,521
DETECTIVE PARK JUNYOUNG

133
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:03,024
[Junyoung] The photo below is
Rosebud Restaurant's steak knife.

134
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:12,117
Were you angry Ms. Oh rejected you?

135
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,702
Of course I was.

136
00:08:13,785 --> 00:08:15,704
So you called her back, didn't you?

137
00:08:16,454 --> 00:08:18,164
[♪ ominous music playing]

138
00:08:32,512 --> 00:08:35,056
-You stabbed her with the steak knife.
-What?

139
00:08:35,724 --> 00:08:36,933
Minyeong.

140
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,239
Please don't kill me.

141
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:55,326
[flesh squelches]

142
00:08:57,037 --> 00:08:58,329
[flesh squelching]

143
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:05,837
[blood splatters]

144
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,255
[♪ music swells]

145
00:09:13,845 --> 00:09:15,013
[♪ music fades]

146
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:17,348
What on earth are you talking about?

147
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:20,310
[Hyera] Here.

148
00:09:20,393 --> 00:09:23,063
-This is Room 701, where you stayed.
-That's right.

149
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,025
-We found blood there.
-[gasps softly]

150
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:28,359
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

151
00:09:28,443 --> 00:09:30,612
And signs that the floor had been cleaned.

152
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:37,202
Where is the knife?

153
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:41,831
Wait...

154
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:44,250
You mean...

155
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,377
Minyeong...

156
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:50,673
died in my hotel room?

157
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:53,843
That's exactly what we're saying.

158
00:09:55,512 --> 00:09:57,138
But I... [gags]

159
00:10:00,058 --> 00:10:01,392
I slept there.

160
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:02,852
[thud]

161
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:09,234
Seriously, why is he always passing out?

162
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:11,194
[both sigh]

163
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:14,322
[knock at door]

164
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,283
-[officer] Did you call?
-[Hyera] Yes.

165
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:19,494
Please lock him up when he's awake.

166
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:26,960
Is he okay?

167
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:29,629
He's fine. He'll wake up
if you give him some water.

168
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,551
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

169
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:38,429
Hello.

170
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:39,514
I'm with the police.

171
00:10:40,223 --> 00:10:41,224
Right.

172
00:10:41,850 --> 00:10:43,226
By any chance,

173
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:47,063
do you remember this guest?

174
00:10:47,147 --> 00:10:48,273
Ah...

175
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:49,357
I do.

176
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:52,861
Did he come here on the night of the 13th?

177
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:53,945
Yes.

178
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:57,323
I was supposed to get off at 8:00 p.m.,

179
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:59,909
but the night staff didn't show,
so I was stuck on duty.

180
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,668
I had plans, but I couldn't make it.

181
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:12,005
What time was that?

182
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:16,134
It was a little before 8:30 p.m.

183
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:19,053
Around 8:20.

184
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:22,515
KEY SUSPECTS
KANG CHUNSIK

185
00:11:22,599 --> 00:11:24,475
YEOM JAESEOP, CHA SERAN, YEOM KIJOO

186
00:11:24,559 --> 00:11:26,811
I really don't think it's Chunsik.

187
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,272
[cell phone vibrating]

188
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:33,359
Hello?

189
00:11:34,152 --> 00:11:36,029
He came to the bar around 8:20 p.m.

190
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:37,113
Got it.

191
00:11:37,822 --> 00:11:39,616
-[line disconnects]
-Pull up the bar hallway.

192
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:41,075
[mouse clicking]

193
00:11:41,159 --> 00:11:42,702
[♪ music increases in tempo]

194
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,330
[keyboard key clacks]

195
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,292
[sighs softly]

196
00:11:53,463 --> 00:11:54,839
Oh, there he is.

197
00:11:56,174 --> 00:11:59,344
[sighs] It doesn't look like
Chunsik's our guy.

198
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:02,305
He may not look like it,
but he's a good kid.

199
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,270
He killed the victim in a fit of rage,

200
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:14,817
went up to the bar for a drink,

201
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:21,574
returned to get rid of the body,

202
00:12:25,995 --> 00:12:27,580
and wiped the floor.

203
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:32,669
Kang Chunsik is the only one
who can do that.

204
00:12:33,336 --> 00:12:34,921
Then how did he move the body?

205
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:36,965
Did he carry her?

206
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:44,973
And even if he knew about
Room 709 through the rumors,

207
00:12:45,056 --> 00:12:47,058
how would he get in?
He doesn't have a key.

208
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:49,477
He could've called someone to do it.

209
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,824
[sighs] Without the camera,
we can't confirm anything.

210
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,617
Did you check all the footage?

211
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:07,203
No, not even half.
There's too much to go through.

212
00:13:07,996 --> 00:13:10,415
-Let's split it. Send it over.
-Yes, ma'am.

213
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:12,250
Time of death was around 8:00 to 9:00 p.m.

214
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:15,545
We have to find everyone
who entered the hotel, took the elevator,

215
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:17,839
or got off on the seventh floor
during that time.

216
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:18,923
Understood.

217
00:13:24,012 --> 00:13:26,055
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

218
00:13:26,139 --> 00:13:27,682
DETECTIVE DIVISION

219
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:31,519
[keyboard key clacks]

220
00:13:35,273 --> 00:13:36,274
[mouse clicks]

221
00:13:37,608 --> 00:13:38,985
Aren't you guys hungry?

222
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,737
Let's order some food.

223
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,239
I'll order it. How about a sandwich?

224
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:45,950
Sounds good. I'll get a beef sandwich.

225
00:13:46,034 --> 00:13:47,910
Beef.

226
00:13:47,994 --> 00:13:49,704
[♪ quirky music playing]

227
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:51,622
Detective Joo?

228
00:13:51,706 --> 00:13:53,207
I'll get the Italian B.M.T.

229
00:13:53,291 --> 00:13:54,417
Ooh.

230
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,794
Italian B.M.T.

231
00:14:01,090 --> 00:14:02,800
This is yours, bro.

232
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:06,929
-This is Detective Joo's.
-[in English] Thank you.

233
00:14:07,889 --> 00:14:11,142
Beef sandwich is the way to go.

234
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:12,351
It's stuffed with meat.

235
00:14:12,435 --> 00:14:14,312
[in Korean] You need ham in a sandwich.

236
00:14:15,188 --> 00:14:17,398
[sighs] We never see eye to eye.

237
00:14:17,482 --> 00:14:19,067
They're both delicious.

238
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:23,946
[Taegyun] Detective Joo!

239
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:25,615
-What...
-Yes?

240
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:27,784
[♪ music fades]

241
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:29,285
You're all...

242
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:30,912
Can I have a word?

243
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:31,996
Yes, sir.

244
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,501
What was that?

245
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:40,088
-Did you arrest the heir of Chunsik Food?
-Yes.

246
00:14:40,171 --> 00:14:41,380
Is he definitely guilty?

247
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:44,300
He's our prime suspect so far.

248
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,968
He also fled, so we arrested him.

249
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:47,762
What if he's innocent? Huh?

250
00:14:48,471 --> 00:14:50,139
Are you going to make me look bad?

251
00:14:50,223 --> 00:14:51,432
Do the reporters know?

252
00:14:51,516 --> 00:14:53,518
What will you do if he's not the culprit?

253
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:55,520
Sir.

254
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,772
Why are you so worried?

255
00:14:57,855 --> 00:15:01,859
If it's not him, I'll handle it.
I'm friends with his dad. We're mutuals.

256
00:15:01,943 --> 00:15:02,985
[♪ jaunty music playing]

257
00:15:03,069 --> 00:15:06,572
[sighs] In any case, just get it right!

258
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:08,074
Get it right!

259
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:11,828
Gosh,

260
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:15,164
how did someone so timid
become a police chief, huh?

261
00:15:15,832 --> 00:15:16,833
[sighs softly]

262
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:18,626
[chuckles softly]

263
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:19,877
[scoffs softly]

264
00:15:19,961 --> 00:15:21,337
[♪ music fades]

265
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,298
SEWON HOSPITAL

266
00:15:24,382 --> 00:15:26,050
KANG JINKYUNG
HEMATOLOGIST-ONCOLOGIST

267
00:15:27,385 --> 00:15:28,427
[mouse clicks]

268
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:30,972
[knock at door]

269
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:32,181
Yes, come in.

270
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:35,643
[door closes]

271
00:15:36,811 --> 00:15:37,812
Mr. Choi Jeonghun?

272
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:40,273
Please have a seat.

273
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:44,026
[sighs]

274
00:15:48,406 --> 00:15:50,158
I've gone over your test results,

275
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:52,410
and there's a malignant tumor
in your stomach.

276
00:15:53,828 --> 00:15:55,580
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

277
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:57,623
Uh, right.

278
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,501
Don't worry too much. We can treat it.

279
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:06,007
Uh, the tumor isn't that large,

280
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,760
but I think surgery will be necessary.

281
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:14,140
-Uh...
-Please don't overthink it.

282
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:18,895
It's just like a car accident
that could happen to anyone.

283
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,900
I'll help you get better.

284
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:35,494
-[chuckles softly]
-[♪ music fades]

285
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:44,795
[clicks tongue]

286
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:49,175
[exhales shakily]

287
00:16:51,177 --> 00:16:52,553
[cell phone vibrating]

288
00:16:54,889 --> 00:16:56,432
DETECTIVE JIN ISOO

289
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,686
-Hello?
-[Isoo] Mr. Choi.

290
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:02,355
Did you go to the hospital?

291
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:04,523
Yes, I'm there now.

292
00:17:04,607 --> 00:17:08,486
-Did you get checked out?
-Yes. They said everything's fine.

293
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,863
[sighs in relief] That's a relief.

294
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:13,950
I was scared that you were seriously ill.

295
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:16,202
What's there to be scared about?

296
00:17:16,285 --> 00:17:18,537
You're the only family I have now.

297
00:17:18,621 --> 00:17:20,539
Don't get sick, okay?

298
00:17:20,623 --> 00:17:23,125
Eat only the good stuff. No whiskey.

299
00:17:23,209 --> 00:17:25,002
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

300
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:26,629
All right.

301
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:30,716
You promised,
so it's your turn to see a psychiatrist.

302
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:33,844
Okay, fine.
I'll go after catching the killer.

303
00:17:33,928 --> 00:17:35,054
Gotta go.

304
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:36,138
All right.

305
00:17:40,518 --> 00:17:41,561
[clicks tongue]

306
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:44,230
[sighs wearily]

307
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:48,276
[♪ music swells, fades]

308
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,659
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

309
00:17:58,411 --> 00:17:59,912
The forensic results are here.

310
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:08,004
The one who asked Yeom Jaeseop
to meet in Room 709 was Ms. Oh Minyeong.

311
00:18:08,796 --> 00:18:10,131
They spoke several times.

312
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:13,092
Yeom transferred
100 million won to her twice.

313
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:14,635
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

314
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,557
[Minyeong] Come to Room 709.

315
00:18:20,099 --> 00:18:22,351
These texts sound a little strange.

316
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:23,894
Where is Yeom Jaeseop right now?

317
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:25,229
Kyungjin is tracking him.

318
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,481
Yeom Jaeseop left the country!

319
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,191
Where did he go?

320
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:31,986
[panting] Hanoi. He just got on board.

321
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:47,543
[♪ music increases in tempo]

322
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:55,009
If he disappears, we can't find him.

323
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:57,511
Contact Hanoi Airport and
get immigration...

324
00:18:57,595 --> 00:18:58,596
[♪ music fades]

325
00:18:58,679 --> 00:18:59,680
Oh.

326
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:01,265
You have a private jet.

327
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:04,101
How did you know about that?

328
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:05,519
I saw it on the news.

329
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:08,314
-Can you catch up with him?
-[in English] Of course!

330
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:09,398
[in Korean] Let's go!

331
00:19:09,482 --> 00:19:11,525
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

332
00:19:20,326 --> 00:19:21,702
[engine roaring]

333
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:24,038
[tires screech]

334
00:19:25,331 --> 00:19:26,666
Come on, run!

335
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:30,461
Captain!

336
00:19:31,212 --> 00:19:32,463
We're off to Hanoi!

337
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:34,965
We have to catch the killer! Hey!

338
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:37,385
Run!

339
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:41,138
[Kyungjin] Detective Joo!
Awesome photo, right?

340
00:19:41,222 --> 00:19:42,682
[Hyera] Am I the only one embarrassed?

341
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:44,225
[Isoo] Just accept it!

342
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:46,727
[Kyungjin] Ta-da!

343
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:49,271
The Hansu private jet.
This is the premium bar.

344
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:51,315
It has all kinds of drinks

345
00:19:51,399 --> 00:19:53,776
and even a fridge. And a kettle, too.

346
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:56,821
Oh, this chair. It's really comfortable.
Try sitting down.

347
00:19:58,781 --> 00:19:59,824
[♪ quirky music playing]

348
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:01,826
-[both sigh contentedly]
-It's nice.

349
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:03,953
When do you use this?

350
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:05,871
Hmm... Whenever.

351
00:20:05,955 --> 00:20:08,958
When I go scuba diving or throw parties.

352
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,460
Ah, I also ride it on December 31st

353
00:20:11,544 --> 00:20:12,837
and follow the setting sun.

354
00:20:14,547 --> 00:20:16,716
Classic rich-people behavior.

355
00:20:16,799 --> 00:20:18,342
It must be nice being rich.

356
00:20:18,426 --> 00:20:19,885
It definitely doesn't hurt.

357
00:20:23,806 --> 00:20:24,932
Hey,

358
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:26,642
how much does this cost?

359
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:27,727
This?

360
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:33,190
-What?
-Makes you jealous, right?

361
00:20:34,442 --> 00:20:36,360
I'll lend it to you when you propose.

362
00:20:36,444 --> 00:20:38,070
-Really?
-Yes.

363
00:20:38,154 --> 00:20:40,072
I love you, bro.

364
00:20:40,156 --> 00:20:42,158
-[chuckles]
-[Isoo] Mmm. Yeah, me too.

365
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,784
You promised.

366
00:20:43,868 --> 00:20:45,911
-Promise.
-Okay, for god's sake.

367
00:20:45,995 --> 00:20:47,747
You all heard, right? [chuckles]

368
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,040
Hey.

369
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:53,586
Would you lend it to me, too?

370
00:20:55,129 --> 00:20:56,338
You want to get married?

371
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:58,257
Are you going to propose?

372
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,510
No, I mean,

373
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:03,095
if the time comes.

374
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:04,764
You thought that far ahead?

375
00:21:04,847 --> 00:21:06,557
Isn't it a little too soon?

376
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:08,851
[clears throat] Hey, I'll make a great MC.

377
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:11,270
[clears throat] We will
now begin the wedding

378
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:13,814
of Groom Park Junyoung
and Bride Yoon Jiwon.

379
00:21:13,898 --> 00:21:15,941
-Please welcome...
-Our groom!

380
00:21:17,026 --> 00:21:18,360
Oh?

381
00:21:19,487 --> 00:21:20,780
I'm going to the restroom.

382
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:24,241
[vocalizing the "Wedding March"]

383
00:21:24,325 --> 00:21:25,951
The restroom's up front.

384
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:27,912
Stupid.

385
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,080
[♪ music fades]

386
00:21:30,164 --> 00:21:32,458
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

387
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:43,552
[♪ music swells, fades]

388
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:48,182
[flight attendant, over PA]
Ladies and gentlemen,

389
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:50,100
we have arrived
at Noi Bai International Airport.

390
00:21:50,184 --> 00:21:51,602
VIETNAM
HANOI AIRPORT

391
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,911
[siren blaring]

392
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:12,122
[Isoo, in English, over megaphone]
Ladies and gentlemen!

393
00:22:12,206 --> 00:22:15,000
This is Jin Isoo Air!

394
00:22:15,084 --> 00:22:18,003
[in Korean] We are urgently looking
for Mr. Yeom Jaeseop!

395
00:22:18,087 --> 00:22:19,088
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

396
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:20,464
I repeat,

397
00:22:20,548 --> 00:22:24,093
we are urgently looking
for Mr. Yeom Jaeseop!

398
00:22:24,885 --> 00:22:27,263
Would Mr. Yeom Jaeseop
please have his passport ready

399
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:30,057
and transfer to this aircraft.

400
00:22:30,808 --> 00:22:33,143
Jin Isoo is here!

401
00:22:33,227 --> 00:22:35,104
Mr. Yeom Jaeseop!

402
00:22:37,314 --> 00:22:38,440
[♪ music fades]

403
00:22:38,524 --> 00:22:41,026
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

404
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:42,903
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

405
00:22:44,405 --> 00:22:47,575
You met Ms. Oh Minyeong at 7:50 p.m.
on the day of the murder.

406
00:22:50,828 --> 00:22:53,622
Just come clean.
We've already checked everything.

407
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:56,458
[sighs softly]

408
00:22:56,542 --> 00:22:58,127
Why did you meet her?

409
00:22:58,210 --> 00:23:00,963
Because of my wife.
I needed to talk to her.

410
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,715
What did you talk about?

411
00:23:03,799 --> 00:23:06,552
She was angry after your wife grabbed
her by the hair, right?

412
00:23:08,387 --> 00:23:09,388
Yes.

413
00:23:10,598 --> 00:23:12,474
So I tried to make it up to her.

414
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:14,894
I'm sorry.

415
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:16,812
Whatever.

416
00:23:16,896 --> 00:23:20,232
When the new hotel opens up,
I'll make you a manager there.

417
00:23:20,316 --> 00:23:22,526
-Really?
-Of course.

418
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:23,777
Oh, you.

419
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:26,030
-[doorbell rings]
-[Seran] Jaeseop!

420
00:23:26,113 --> 00:23:27,239
[banging on door]

421
00:23:27,323 --> 00:23:29,116
-Are you in there?
-[doorbell rings]

422
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:32,328
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

423
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:35,039
[whispering] I'll go first,
so you can come out later.

424
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:42,212
I didn't see her after that.

425
00:23:42,296 --> 00:23:43,839
What time was that?

426
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:46,759
[sighs softly]

427
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:50,930
I think it was around 8:00 p.m.

428
00:23:52,765 --> 00:23:55,893
What did you do before going back
to your office at 8:20 p.m.?

429
00:23:55,976 --> 00:23:57,770
I was on the phone, at the stairwell.

430
00:23:57,853 --> 00:24:00,230
At the stairwell? With whom?

431
00:24:00,314 --> 00:24:01,565
It was a business call.

432
00:24:06,737 --> 00:24:08,489
OH MINYEONG BANK STATEMENT

433
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:10,324
You gave Ms. Oh 200 million won.

434
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:15,120
100 million two months ago,
and another 100 million last week.

435
00:24:15,204 --> 00:24:17,039
It was a form of compensation.

436
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:19,124
Because my wife hit her.

437
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:21,794
Oh, he must be really well-off.

438
00:24:21,877 --> 00:24:22,878
Two hundred million won.

439
00:24:23,379 --> 00:24:24,546
[sighs]

440
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:26,256
Are you going to keep lying?

441
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:30,260
She blackmailed you, didn't she?

442
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:32,137
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

443
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:36,558
[Minyeong] When are you
going to send me the money?

444
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:39,103
If you keep this up,
you're going to regret it.

445
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:41,230
"Do not test my patience."

446
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:43,565
[sighs defeatedly, clicks tongue]

447
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:45,484
[Hyera] What's the reason?

448
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:47,569
Why did she blackmail you?

449
00:24:48,821 --> 00:24:50,739
That has nothing to do with this case.

450
00:24:50,823 --> 00:24:52,241
That's for us to decide.

451
00:24:53,701 --> 00:24:56,161
You'd had enough of the blackmail,
so you killed her.

452
00:24:56,245 --> 00:24:57,496
That's not true.

453
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:59,915
She was definitely alive
when I left the room.

454
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,710
If she were killed in that room,

455
00:25:04,086 --> 00:25:06,547
it means someone was trying to frame me.

456
00:25:06,630 --> 00:25:08,090
[♪ music swells]

457
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:16,640
[♪ music fades]

458
00:25:16,724 --> 00:25:18,142
Open your eyes.

459
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:19,935
Open your eyes wide.

460
00:25:21,645 --> 00:25:23,605
Mmm. [in English] Okay.

461
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,066
"Leo"?

462
00:25:27,234 --> 00:25:28,360
[in Korean] Who's Leo?

463
00:25:29,111 --> 00:25:31,488
Leonardo DiCa... Him?

464
00:25:32,072 --> 00:25:33,991
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

465
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,621
ROSEBUD HOTEL STAFF ROSTER

466
00:25:45,419 --> 00:25:46,462
FRONT DESK JEON YUJIN

467
00:25:47,963 --> 00:25:49,590
EMPLOYEE RECORD

468
00:25:49,673 --> 00:25:51,925
It's him. Jeon Yujin.

469
00:25:53,635 --> 00:25:54,887
NAME JEON YUJIN

470
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,597
Right, Mr. Jeon Yujin.

471
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,557
He was the one in the CEO's office.

472
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:00,642
-Check the camera outside the office.
-[Kyungjin] Okay.

473
00:26:00,726 --> 00:26:02,144
[keyboard clacking]

474
00:26:08,609 --> 00:26:09,902
[mouse clicking]

475
00:26:12,196 --> 00:26:13,447
[♪ music increases in tempo]

476
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:14,531
[keyboard keys clacking]

477
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:19,745
-[keyboard key clacks]
-[Kyungjin] That's a bit strange.

478
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:21,163
[keyboard key clacks]

479
00:26:23,665 --> 00:26:25,834
What employee barges
into the CEO's office?

480
00:26:26,502 --> 00:26:27,753
We have a new suspect.

481
00:26:29,338 --> 00:26:30,798
The CEO's mistress.

482
00:26:31,799 --> 00:26:33,801
No, his male lover.

483
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:40,265
[♪ music swells, stops]

484
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:43,018
Mr. Yeom.

485
00:26:44,103 --> 00:26:47,439
The one you love is Jeon Yujin, isn't it?

486
00:26:49,316 --> 00:26:50,400
[sighs defeatedly]

487
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,960
I didn't know I'd turn out this way.

488
00:27:08,043 --> 00:27:10,671
I'm married, and I even have a kid.

489
00:27:11,213 --> 00:27:12,548
[♪ soft, enthralling music playing]

490
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:14,591
I fell for him like crazy.

491
00:27:15,467 --> 00:27:18,220
TWO MONTHS EARLIER

492
00:27:18,303 --> 00:27:20,013
-Sir.
-Yes, Mr. Yu.

493
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,685
-These are our new employees.
-Ah.

494
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,230
Nice to meet you.

495
00:27:40,701 --> 00:27:41,827
Welcome to our hotel.

496
00:27:48,876 --> 00:27:51,128
-[employee 1] Cheers.
-[employee 2] Cheers.

497
00:27:51,211 --> 00:27:53,171
[♪ gentle music playing]

498
00:27:53,255 --> 00:27:54,548
[meat sizzling]

499
00:27:55,924 --> 00:27:58,176
-Let me pour you one.
-Thank you.

500
00:27:58,260 --> 00:27:59,511
[Yujin] I look forward
to working with you.

501
00:27:59,595 --> 00:28:01,388
Enjoy your food.

502
00:28:04,099 --> 00:28:05,934
Sir, let me pour you a glass, too.

503
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:12,941
[employee 3] Thank you.

504
00:28:13,025 --> 00:28:14,026
Thank you for dinner.

505
00:28:14,109 --> 00:28:15,444
Have a safe trip home.

506
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:17,654
Take care.

507
00:28:18,405 --> 00:28:19,531
Sir...

508
00:28:20,282 --> 00:28:21,491
Watch your step.

509
00:28:24,036 --> 00:28:25,454
Thank you.

510
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:43,639
[♪ music turns suspenseful]

511
00:28:57,319 --> 00:28:58,320
Stop the car.

512
00:28:58,403 --> 00:28:59,446
[car honks]

513
00:29:04,701 --> 00:29:06,662
Get in. I'll take you home.

514
00:29:06,745 --> 00:29:08,038
[♪ music swells]

515
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:14,211
[♪ music fades]

516
00:29:21,343 --> 00:29:22,344
Dry yourself.

517
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:38,318
[♪ gentle music playing]

518
00:30:06,596 --> 00:30:08,515
Don't start anything if you're not sure.

519
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:11,226
I don't want to get hurt anymore.

520
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:15,022
Yujin.

521
00:30:19,443 --> 00:30:20,944
Even if you're an alien,

522
00:30:21,570 --> 00:30:22,571
or a man...

523
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:26,158
I really don't know anymore. [sighs]

524
00:30:29,369 --> 00:30:30,954
Let's see this through to the end.

525
00:30:41,798 --> 00:30:43,050
[♪ music fades]

526
00:30:43,133 --> 00:30:44,718
[inhales sharply]

527
00:30:44,801 --> 00:30:46,970
We met secretly in Room 709.

528
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:48,597
[glasses clink]

529
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:50,474
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

530
00:30:54,352 --> 00:30:56,438
Mmm. It's good.

531
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:57,773
Yes, it's delicious.

532
00:30:58,356 --> 00:30:59,733
Do you like wine?

533
00:30:59,816 --> 00:31:01,234
Oh, I do.

534
00:31:01,318 --> 00:31:02,569
[Jaeseop] It felt like a dream.

535
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:04,321
But...

536
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:06,907
it didn't last long.

537
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:35,143
[door closes]

538
00:31:45,821 --> 00:31:47,781
[Jaeseop] Then the blackmail started.

539
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:02,629
[scoffs] Mr. Yeom.

540
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:06,800
Why are you so cheap?

541
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:09,302
You really think this is enough?

542
00:32:09,386 --> 00:32:10,929
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

543
00:32:11,012 --> 00:32:12,097
[sighs wearily]

544
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:14,432
So I sent her 100 million won.

545
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:18,895
Then my wife caused a scene,
so I sent her another 100 million.

546
00:32:19,855 --> 00:32:23,108
But that day,
she said she wanted to see me.

547
00:32:23,692 --> 00:32:24,776
[door opens]

548
00:32:26,528 --> 00:32:27,571
[door closes]

549
00:32:28,405 --> 00:32:29,489
[sighs wearily]

550
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:32,993
Minyeong, what do you want me to do?

551
00:32:34,161 --> 00:32:35,871
[sighs] My feet are killing me.

552
00:32:37,372 --> 00:32:38,373
[sighs wearily]

553
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:41,168
I think I might quit.

554
00:32:42,377 --> 00:32:44,045
I don't want to come into work,

555
00:32:44,921 --> 00:32:47,048
and I'm sick of all the annoying guests.

556
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:52,554
Mr. Yeom.

557
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,139
I'd like a leaving bonus.

558
00:32:57,100 --> 00:32:58,810
I don't have any money.

559
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:02,522
If you don't have money,
what does that make me?

560
00:33:04,191 --> 00:33:05,192
[doorbell rings]

561
00:33:05,275 --> 00:33:06,484
[Seran] Honey! Get out here!

562
00:33:06,568 --> 00:33:07,777
[Seran] Are you in there?

563
00:33:07,861 --> 00:33:09,446
Where are you?

564
00:33:09,529 --> 00:33:10,572
Look who's busted.

565
00:33:11,156 --> 00:33:12,324
[Seran] Come out here!

566
00:33:12,407 --> 00:33:13,450
Shall I open the door?

567
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:16,328
[Jaeseop] Wait.

568
00:33:17,829 --> 00:33:19,915
Okay, fine.

569
00:33:20,624 --> 00:33:21,833
I want one billion won.

570
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:24,336
I need time.

571
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:28,131
Will a month do?

572
00:33:29,466 --> 00:33:32,719
Mr. Yeom, I'm going
to take leave starting tomorrow.

573
00:33:32,802 --> 00:33:34,763
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

574
00:33:37,140 --> 00:33:38,141
[Jaeseop sighs wearily]

575
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,105
[line connects, ringing]

576
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:49,110
Yujin. [sighs wearily]

577
00:33:51,196 --> 00:33:52,280
Let's end this.

578
00:33:55,408 --> 00:33:57,911
What's wrong?
Did Oh Minyeong blackmail you again?

579
00:33:57,994 --> 00:34:00,872
There's nothing more to say. Let's end it.

580
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:02,666
I told you not to start if you're unsure.

581
00:34:02,749 --> 00:34:04,584
You said you'd see it through.

582
00:34:04,668 --> 00:34:07,295
This is the end! Don't you get it?

583
00:34:07,379 --> 00:34:09,214
Then what am I supposed to do?

584
00:34:09,297 --> 00:34:11,341
How can I work here
when I have to see you?

585
00:34:11,424 --> 00:34:13,802
Then you leave! You can just quit!

586
00:34:15,595 --> 00:34:16,721
Jaeseop.

587
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:18,390
[door closes]

588
00:34:22,310 --> 00:34:23,311
[door slams]

589
00:34:24,312 --> 00:34:25,480
[sighs regretfully]

590
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:27,148
Then why did you flee?

591
00:34:28,316 --> 00:34:30,485
When I heard Oh Minyeong had died,

592
00:34:31,403 --> 00:34:32,904
I had a bad feeling.

593
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:34,489
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

594
00:34:35,156 --> 00:34:37,367
Had Yujin killed her?

595
00:34:37,951 --> 00:34:39,452
No, it couldn't be.

596
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:42,956
But when I heard she died in Room 709,

597
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:45,417
I thought Yujin had killed her
in that room

598
00:34:46,001 --> 00:34:48,128
to get revenge on me.

599
00:34:50,547 --> 00:34:52,173
I didn't know what to do,

600
00:34:53,967 --> 00:34:55,802
so I just ran away.

601
00:34:56,428 --> 00:34:58,597
Is this something
you can just run away from?

602
00:35:00,724 --> 00:35:01,725
[♪ music fades]

603
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:02,809
By the way,

604
00:35:04,269 --> 00:35:05,687
why is it "Leo"?

605
00:35:07,939 --> 00:35:09,899
It's Yujin's zodiac sign.

606
00:35:10,734 --> 00:35:12,068
Ah.

607
00:35:12,152 --> 00:35:13,194
His zodiac sign.

608
00:35:14,154 --> 00:35:17,073
Right, you're quite the romantic.

609
00:35:17,157 --> 00:35:18,533
-Ah.
-[inhales softly]

610
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:20,619
-[exhales deeply]
-[Isoo] His zodiac sign.

611
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:25,915
How did it go?

612
00:35:25,999 --> 00:35:28,209
It was a tragic love story.

613
00:35:28,752 --> 00:35:30,754
It touched my heart. Ah.

614
00:35:31,338 --> 00:35:33,340
Let's look into Jeon Yujin.

615
00:35:33,423 --> 00:35:35,634
Kyungjin, trace his movements on that day.

616
00:35:35,717 --> 00:35:37,802
-And find out where he is now.
-Got it.

617
00:35:42,015 --> 00:35:43,850
[handcuffs clinking]

618
00:35:45,477 --> 00:35:46,519
[handcuffs click open]

619
00:35:47,354 --> 00:35:49,564
-[officer] Take out all your belongings.
-[handcuffs jingle]

620
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:54,319
[Chunsik] Mr. Yeom.

621
00:35:54,903 --> 00:35:55,987
Did you...

622
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:59,240
kill Minyeong?

623
00:35:59,324 --> 00:36:00,659
[♪ quirky dramatic music playing]

624
00:36:02,827 --> 00:36:05,830
It was you, asshole.
You killed her, didn't you?

625
00:36:05,914 --> 00:36:07,082
Come here.

626
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:08,583
[clanging]

627
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:10,835
[yelling] Come here right now!

628
00:36:10,919 --> 00:36:14,547
[sobbing] Do you have
any idea how much I loved her?

629
00:36:14,631 --> 00:36:16,716
Kang Chunsik! Get back.

630
00:36:17,967 --> 00:36:20,387
What are you going to do about Minyeong?

631
00:36:21,137 --> 00:36:24,015
What are you going to do about me?

632
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:25,642
[sobbing]

633
00:36:28,103 --> 00:36:29,187
[♪ music fades]

634
00:36:29,270 --> 00:36:30,522
[Isoo sighs softly]

635
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:38,655
-[keyboard key clacks]
-Jeon Yujin answered the call at 8:05 p.m.

636
00:36:40,448 --> 00:36:41,449
Hello?

637
00:36:41,533 --> 00:36:42,909
[Jaeseop] Yujin. [sighs wearily]

638
00:36:42,992 --> 00:36:44,786
Let's end this.

639
00:36:44,869 --> 00:36:46,287
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

640
00:36:48,289 --> 00:36:51,126
[Kyungjin] He left the CEO's office
and went to the bar.

641
00:36:55,964 --> 00:36:57,048
[tremulous exhale]

642
00:37:02,137 --> 00:37:04,055
He must've seen Chunsik there.

643
00:37:04,139 --> 00:37:06,599
He would've thought of using Room 701.

644
00:37:06,683 --> 00:37:10,437
Because it was well-known
that Kang Chunsik liked Ms. Oh.

645
00:37:11,020 --> 00:37:12,731
I found the last footage of Ms. Oh.

646
00:37:12,814 --> 00:37:14,149
I think she was on the roof.

647
00:37:15,734 --> 00:37:18,194
She got on the staff elevator at 8:40 p.m.

648
00:37:26,161 --> 00:37:29,247
She must have hidden out
on the roof to avoid Mr. Yeom's wife.

649
00:37:38,757 --> 00:37:40,133
Fifteen minutes.

650
00:37:41,009 --> 00:37:42,761
Where was Jeon Yujin during this time?

651
00:37:43,845 --> 00:37:45,096
[mouse clicks]

652
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,142
Back to the changing room.

653
00:38:07,994 --> 00:38:10,705
He must've gone to get
his radio and the master key.

654
00:38:10,789 --> 00:38:12,791
This was when he decided to kill her.

655
00:38:15,877 --> 00:38:16,920
[card reader beeps]

656
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:19,380
[Isoo] He snuck into Room 701.

657
00:38:21,049 --> 00:38:22,258
Ms. Oh.

658
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:24,469
A call came in from Room 701.

659
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:26,888
[Isoo] He told her
Chunsik had called for her.

660
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:29,766
[♪ music swells, fades]

661
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:36,231
[sighs deeply] All we have is the motive.

662
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:38,191
No murder weapon,

663
00:38:38,900 --> 00:38:41,027
and the radio call
wouldn't have been logged.

664
00:38:43,154 --> 00:38:44,948
Where's Jeon Yujin after that?

665
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:46,741
[keyboard keys clacking]

666
00:38:47,742 --> 00:38:48,743
The elevator.

667
00:38:48,827 --> 00:38:50,578
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

668
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:58,169
There's only an eight-minute gap.

669
00:38:59,963 --> 00:39:02,924
In that time, he killed the victim,

670
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:05,051
moved the body, and cleaned up?

671
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:06,511
That's impossible, isn't it?

672
00:39:07,178 --> 00:39:09,931
-It's impossible, without an accomplice.
-No, wait.

673
00:39:11,224 --> 00:39:12,934
Why move the body?

674
00:39:13,977 --> 00:39:15,395
He saw Chunsik at the bar

675
00:39:18,314 --> 00:39:21,484
and called her to Room 701
to dump it on Chunsik.

676
00:39:21,568 --> 00:39:22,902
[♪ pensive music playing]

677
00:39:22,986 --> 00:39:23,987
That's true.

678
00:39:24,696 --> 00:39:26,322
There's no reason to move the body.

679
00:39:26,406 --> 00:39:27,866
What if after killing her,

680
00:39:27,949 --> 00:39:30,827
he wanted to get revenge
on Yeom Jaeseop and moved the body?

681
00:39:31,578 --> 00:39:34,539
No, that can't be done in eight minutes.

682
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:35,999
[inhales sharply]

683
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:38,501
This wasn't a premeditated murder.

684
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:41,129
How can there be an accomplice?

685
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:43,756
What on earth could have happened?

686
00:39:44,757 --> 00:39:47,844
Who moved the body and even cleaned up?

687
00:39:53,725 --> 00:39:57,312
Someone who knows
that the security camera was broken.

688
00:39:57,979 --> 00:40:00,231
Someone who can move
without drawing attention

689
00:40:00,315 --> 00:40:03,735
and move the body
without raising any suspicion.

690
00:40:04,527 --> 00:40:06,613
Someone who has access to all the rooms.

691
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:09,616
Someone who can clean perfectly.

692
00:40:13,453 --> 00:40:15,580
-Housekeeping.
-[gasps] No way.

693
00:40:17,373 --> 00:40:19,042
What about housekeeping?

694
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:23,129
Yeom could've given the order
after finding out Jeon had killed her.

695
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:24,756
[♪ ominous music playing]

696
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:28,551
[breath trembling] I killed her.

697
00:40:30,553 --> 00:40:31,554
I...

698
00:40:32,805 --> 00:40:34,265
I ended up killing her.

699
00:40:35,934 --> 00:40:37,101
I'll take care of it.

700
00:40:38,728 --> 00:40:40,021
Get out of there right now.

701
00:40:40,104 --> 00:40:41,981
In the room he personally used?

702
00:40:42,941 --> 00:40:45,693
He probably hid the body first
to deal with later.

703
00:40:48,029 --> 00:40:50,990
We'll go to the hotel,
so identify the housekeeping staff.

704
00:40:51,074 --> 00:40:53,201
And find out where Jeon dumped his jacket.

705
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:54,619
-[Kyungjin] Understood.
-Okay.

706
00:40:54,702 --> 00:40:56,371
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

707
00:40:59,999 --> 00:41:01,960
How could it be one of those ladies?

708
00:41:02,043 --> 00:41:03,753
-It's so good.
-It's really delicious.

709
00:41:03,836 --> 00:41:05,588
Now I see why it's 100,000 won.

710
00:41:05,672 --> 00:41:07,548
Is there anyone you can rule out?

711
00:41:09,884 --> 00:41:10,885
There is.

712
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:15,264
Gosh, you keep calling us ladies
and flattering us like that.

713
00:41:15,348 --> 00:41:19,018
[sighs] If that was an act,
she deserves an Oscar.

714
00:41:19,102 --> 00:41:20,561
[♪ music fades]

715
00:41:20,645 --> 00:41:21,646
[Isoo scoffs]

716
00:41:29,904 --> 00:41:31,280
There you are.

717
00:41:31,364 --> 00:41:33,324
What? What is it?

718
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:35,410
Did you find the killer?

719
00:41:35,493 --> 00:41:36,828
Uh, well...

720
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:39,080
-We have something to ask you.
-What is it?

721
00:41:39,998 --> 00:41:41,833
Were any of the housekeeping staff

722
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:44,961
acting suspiciously on the day
of the murder or the next day?

723
00:41:45,044 --> 00:41:47,255
What? Us, the housekeeping staff?

724
00:41:48,131 --> 00:41:49,549
What are you talking about?

725
00:41:50,258 --> 00:41:53,761
Someone moved Ms. Oh Minyeong's body.

726
00:41:53,845 --> 00:41:55,972
[stutters] Someone
from the housekeeping staff?

727
00:41:56,681 --> 00:41:57,890
Who?

728
00:41:58,558 --> 00:42:00,143
It's a possibility.

729
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:02,645
Did anyone seem odd?

730
00:42:03,312 --> 00:42:04,647
Oh... [mutters]

731
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:07,191
[gasps]

732
00:42:07,859 --> 00:42:08,860
What is it?

733
00:42:08,943 --> 00:42:10,403
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

734
00:42:11,529 --> 00:42:13,740
She was cleaning the cart.

735
00:42:13,823 --> 00:42:15,408
She said she spilled coffee on it.

736
00:42:20,288 --> 00:42:21,414
My gosh.

737
00:42:21,497 --> 00:42:23,458
-[chuckles nervously]
-What are you doing?

738
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:24,917
I spilled some coffee.

739
00:42:25,001 --> 00:42:26,544
-Really?
-Yes.

740
00:42:26,627 --> 00:42:27,628
You startled me.

741
00:42:27,712 --> 00:42:30,381
You should clock out.
I'll tidy up in here.

742
00:42:30,465 --> 00:42:32,133
-Okay.
-Bye.

743
00:42:37,555 --> 00:42:39,098
We found her. It's Na Yeonhong.

744
00:42:39,182 --> 00:42:40,558
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

745
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:41,851
EMPLOYEE RECORD
NA YEONHONG

746
00:42:43,436 --> 00:42:44,520
SON: JEON YUJIN

747
00:42:44,604 --> 00:42:45,813
She's Jeon Yujin's mom.

748
00:42:48,107 --> 00:42:49,150
[line disconnects]

749
00:42:51,194 --> 00:42:52,361
She's Jeon Yujin's mom.

750
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:56,199
She knew her son killed someone
and covered it up.

751
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:00,620
-[door opens]
-[sighs softly]

752
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:11,130
[♪ music swells, stabilizes]

753
00:43:11,214 --> 00:43:12,799
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

754
00:43:24,352 --> 00:43:25,478
[doorbell rings]

755
00:43:33,361 --> 00:43:35,363
[♪ music increases in tempo]

756
00:44:00,555 --> 00:44:01,889
[♪ music swells]

757
00:44:04,267 --> 00:44:05,726
[♪ music stabilizes]

758
00:44:06,602 --> 00:44:08,187
[breathes tremulously]

759
00:44:08,271 --> 00:44:09,272
[gasps]

760
00:44:16,237 --> 00:44:17,530
[gasping]

761
00:44:19,574 --> 00:44:20,950
[breathing frantically]

762
00:44:21,033 --> 00:44:22,493
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

763
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:25,663
[crying]

764
00:44:28,416 --> 00:44:29,417
[exclaims]

765
00:44:32,086 --> 00:44:33,337
[sobbing]

766
00:44:41,804 --> 00:44:43,222
[hyperventilating]

767
00:44:43,306 --> 00:44:45,224
[♪ music increases in tempo]

768
00:44:45,308 --> 00:44:46,559
[catches breath]

769
00:44:49,812 --> 00:44:51,105
[grunts, exclaims]

770
00:45:07,914 --> 00:45:09,248
[breathing frantically]

771
00:45:13,586 --> 00:45:15,213
MINYEONG

772
00:45:15,296 --> 00:45:16,797
-[continues breathing frantically]
-[bottle spraying]

773
00:45:16,881 --> 00:45:19,342
We'll find evidence if we check the cart.

774
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:21,302
Let's arrest Ms. Na Yeonhong first.

775
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:22,762
Wait.

776
00:45:24,013 --> 00:45:25,264
Let me talk to her first.

777
00:45:26,098 --> 00:45:27,516
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

778
00:45:46,285 --> 00:45:47,286
[♪ music fades]

779
00:45:47,370 --> 00:45:48,871
Something on your mind?

780
00:45:50,790 --> 00:45:52,416
No, nothing. [chuckles softly]

781
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:53,960
Would you like some tea?

782
00:45:54,043 --> 00:45:55,336
Thank you.

783
00:45:55,419 --> 00:45:56,879
Here.

784
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:03,052
[exhales softly]

785
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,140
[♪ soft tense music playing]

786
00:46:11,352 --> 00:46:12,895
One moment, please.

787
00:46:24,949 --> 00:46:26,409
[♪ soft, pensive music playing]

788
00:46:26,492 --> 00:46:28,160
[inhales sharply] You must be tired.

789
00:46:28,244 --> 00:46:31,664
I'm fine. [chuckles]
Everyone has to make a living.

790
00:46:33,666 --> 00:46:34,750
My mom

791
00:46:35,918 --> 00:46:37,920
died when I was young.

792
00:46:38,004 --> 00:46:40,506
Gosh, I'm sorry to hear that.

793
00:46:41,590 --> 00:46:43,384
I was lonely, so I acted out

794
00:46:43,467 --> 00:46:45,803
and did a lot of stupid things.

795
00:46:46,470 --> 00:46:47,513
[chuckles softly]

796
00:46:48,264 --> 00:46:50,016
No matter how badly I messed up,

797
00:46:51,100 --> 00:46:52,560
she'd be on my side, right?

798
00:46:52,643 --> 00:46:54,312
Of course.

799
00:46:55,021 --> 00:46:57,732
To a mother,
her child will always be her baby.

800
00:46:59,066 --> 00:47:01,402
There's nothing
she wouldn't do for her child. [chuckles]

801
00:47:02,528 --> 00:47:03,529
You're right.

802
00:47:05,072 --> 00:47:06,949
My mom would've been the same.

803
00:47:09,994 --> 00:47:11,162
But if I...

804
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:16,459
committed an unforgivable crime,

805
00:47:18,836 --> 00:47:22,006
and if my mom was punished
for trying to protect me,

806
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:25,217
I would probably...

807
00:47:27,345 --> 00:47:29,889
never be able to forgive myself.

808
00:47:34,643 --> 00:47:36,604
Please tell me

809
00:47:38,230 --> 00:47:39,440
what happened.

810
00:47:39,523 --> 00:47:41,400
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

811
00:47:47,656 --> 00:47:49,116
I killed her.

812
00:47:51,577 --> 00:47:54,413
This isn't the right thing for Yujin.

813
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,625
Please reconsider.

814
00:48:00,419 --> 00:48:01,504
[crying] I'm sorry.

815
00:48:05,424 --> 00:48:06,425
[♪ music fades]

816
00:48:06,509 --> 00:48:08,177
Please tell the truth.

817
00:48:08,886 --> 00:48:10,763
Everything will come to light in the end.

818
00:48:13,015 --> 00:48:14,517
[♪ gentle, somber music playing]

819
00:48:15,768 --> 00:48:16,852
[sniffles]

820
00:48:17,645 --> 00:48:19,438
I killed Ms. Oh Minyeong.

821
00:48:25,152 --> 00:48:26,153
Get up.

822
00:48:36,580 --> 00:48:37,623
Ms. Na Yeonhong,

823
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:40,543
you're under arrest
for Ms. Oh Minyeong's murder.

824
00:48:40,626 --> 00:48:42,962
-[handcuffs rattle, click]
-You have the right to an attorney

825
00:48:43,045 --> 00:48:45,423
and the right to remain silent.

826
00:48:45,506 --> 00:48:47,675
You won't be penalized
for remaining silent.

827
00:49:08,779 --> 00:49:09,989
[gasps]

828
00:49:10,072 --> 00:49:11,073
Stop right there!

829
00:49:11,157 --> 00:49:12,158
[sobbing]

830
00:49:23,169 --> 00:49:24,211
[exclaims]

831
00:49:25,421 --> 00:49:26,589
[Yujin] Wait!

832
00:49:29,049 --> 00:49:30,092
[gasping] No, Yujin!

833
00:49:31,302 --> 00:49:33,762
-I killed her.
-[sobbing] Yujin!

834
00:49:33,846 --> 00:49:34,972
No.

835
00:49:36,765 --> 00:49:39,018
Yujin...

836
00:49:39,685 --> 00:49:41,395
My mom did nothing wrong.

837
00:49:41,479 --> 00:49:43,230
[Yeonhong] No, Yujin, no.

838
00:49:44,106 --> 00:49:45,149
Yujin, my baby.

839
00:49:45,900 --> 00:49:47,693
[continues sobbing] Yujin, no.

840
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:50,738
Yujin!

841
00:49:52,490 --> 00:49:53,741
No, not you.

842
00:49:55,326 --> 00:49:56,785
-No, Yujin.
-I'm sorry.

843
00:49:56,869 --> 00:49:58,871
My baby.

844
00:50:01,790 --> 00:50:05,294
I was the one who killed her.

845
00:50:05,377 --> 00:50:07,046
[yelling] Me!

846
00:50:07,129 --> 00:50:08,297
Oh, my goodness.

847
00:50:10,966 --> 00:50:13,219
Please, no, my baby.

848
00:50:14,053 --> 00:50:15,888
My baby.

849
00:50:15,971 --> 00:50:17,640
[♪ melancholy music playing]

850
00:50:17,723 --> 00:50:19,517
-[sniffles]
-[continues sobbing]

851
00:50:27,816 --> 00:50:28,817
[Yujin] You're right.

852
00:50:31,070 --> 00:50:33,447
I called her over to Room 701
and killed her.

853
00:50:34,031 --> 00:50:35,157
[slow footsteps approaching]

854
00:50:35,241 --> 00:50:36,700
[♪ ominous music playing]

855
00:50:44,041 --> 00:50:45,042
[door closes]

856
00:51:05,062 --> 00:51:06,105
[sighs]

857
00:51:06,564 --> 00:51:07,690
What are you doing?

858
00:51:07,773 --> 00:51:09,024
Just stop.

859
00:51:09,108 --> 00:51:10,109
[scoffs]

860
00:51:10,734 --> 00:51:11,735
Stop what?

861
00:51:12,444 --> 00:51:13,821
You got your money.

862
00:51:14,488 --> 00:51:15,948
So stop blackmailing us.

863
00:51:19,034 --> 00:51:21,787
I basically struck gold here.

864
00:51:22,538 --> 00:51:24,123
Would you stop if you were me?

865
00:51:27,459 --> 00:51:28,961
[sighs in exasperation]

866
00:51:30,754 --> 00:51:31,755
[breathes shakily]

867
00:51:36,135 --> 00:51:37,136
You...

868
00:51:37,928 --> 00:51:39,221
Are you out of your mind?

869
00:51:39,847 --> 00:51:42,099
Yes, I'm out of my mind.

870
00:51:43,475 --> 00:51:44,685
[flesh squelching]

871
00:51:44,768 --> 00:51:46,145
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

872
00:51:48,731 --> 00:51:49,982
[blood splatters]

873
00:51:55,321 --> 00:51:57,114
[♪ music increases in tempo]

874
00:52:00,993 --> 00:52:02,286
[breath trembling]

875
00:52:02,828 --> 00:52:03,871
[♪ music fades]

876
00:52:03,954 --> 00:52:07,041
Then I heard the body was found
in Room 709,

877
00:52:10,085 --> 00:52:12,296
so I thought
Mr. Yeom had covered up for me.

878
00:52:12,963 --> 00:52:15,007
[♪ gentle melancholy music playing]

879
00:52:15,090 --> 00:52:17,384
[crying] I had no idea it was my mom.

880
00:52:18,636 --> 00:52:20,304
I guess you didn't tell the hotel

881
00:52:21,013 --> 00:52:22,723
you were working with your mother.

882
00:52:23,432 --> 00:52:24,433
No.

883
00:52:26,769 --> 00:52:28,937
She's been working there for a while,

884
00:52:29,021 --> 00:52:30,564
and I...

885
00:52:32,107 --> 00:52:34,026
I started working this year.

886
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:37,446
My mom said we should act like strangers,

887
00:52:37,529 --> 00:52:39,657
because nothing good would come from it.

888
00:52:42,826 --> 00:52:45,663
[sobbing] After she got divorced,
I was all she had.

889
00:52:47,665 --> 00:52:48,707
Because of me...

890
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:50,834
my mom...

891
00:52:54,338 --> 00:52:58,092
All you're worried about is your mom
after you murdered someone?

892
00:53:02,346 --> 00:53:03,639
You're a murderer.

893
00:53:06,600 --> 00:53:08,435
You ended someone's life.

894
00:53:09,436 --> 00:53:11,438
[sniffles, sobbing]

895
00:53:14,108 --> 00:53:16,235
Was it worth all that?

896
00:53:23,534 --> 00:53:24,660
[♪ music fades]

897
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:28,122
[pen scratching]

898
00:53:33,043 --> 00:53:36,422
Mr. Yeom Jaeseop, Mr. Kang Chunsik,
you're cleared of all suspicion.

899
00:53:36,505 --> 00:53:37,506
You are free to go.

900
00:53:41,844 --> 00:53:43,846
-Jaeseop!
-Dad!

901
00:53:43,929 --> 00:53:46,098
[exhales sharply] What happened, huh?

902
00:53:47,391 --> 00:53:48,392
Did you kill her?

903
00:53:49,226 --> 00:53:50,227
No.

904
00:53:50,310 --> 00:53:52,187
Then what?

905
00:53:52,271 --> 00:53:54,022
You're cheating, aren't you?

906
00:53:54,106 --> 00:53:56,191
It's all over. Just stop.

907
00:53:56,275 --> 00:53:57,359
[exhales deeply]

908
00:53:57,443 --> 00:53:59,445
You're a coward until the end.

909
00:53:59,528 --> 00:54:00,904
Why did you even start it?

910
00:54:02,114 --> 00:54:03,198
[sighs regretfully]

911
00:54:05,367 --> 00:54:06,493
It's Leo.

912
00:54:14,835 --> 00:54:16,128
Seran.

913
00:54:18,005 --> 00:54:20,466
Yujin is the one I love.

914
00:54:21,175 --> 00:54:22,426
[♪ quirky music playing]

915
00:54:22,509 --> 00:54:24,136
Yujin?

916
00:54:24,219 --> 00:54:25,637
Wait,

917
00:54:25,721 --> 00:54:27,848
who the hell is Yujin?

918
00:54:33,103 --> 00:54:34,104
Oh, my god.

919
00:54:34,730 --> 00:54:35,981
[gasps softly]

920
00:54:45,532 --> 00:54:47,910
Then why did Minyeong die?

921
00:54:49,786 --> 00:54:52,039
She was a blackmailer.

922
00:54:53,373 --> 00:54:55,459
She blackmailed them and was murdered.

923
00:54:56,418 --> 00:54:58,378
My sweet, angelic Minyeong

924
00:55:00,130 --> 00:55:01,256
was a blackmailer?

925
00:55:01,340 --> 00:55:03,175
Don't pass out, seriously.

926
00:55:03,258 --> 00:55:04,301
Huh?

927
00:55:04,384 --> 00:55:06,011
-[thud]
-[both exclaim]

928
00:55:06,094 --> 00:55:07,429
Kang Chunsik!

929
00:55:08,096 --> 00:55:10,265
[breathing heavily] Now even a man is...

930
00:55:11,016 --> 00:55:12,309
A man... [exclaims]

931
00:55:12,392 --> 00:55:14,686
Come on, seriously?

932
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:17,606
Is passing out contagious now?
What the heck?

933
00:55:17,689 --> 00:55:19,900
For god's sake!

934
00:55:20,651 --> 00:55:22,945
Hello, 119?
Yes, this is Gangha Police Station.

935
00:55:25,447 --> 00:55:26,907
[sighs contentedly]

936
00:55:29,409 --> 00:55:30,536
[sighs in relief]

937
00:55:30,619 --> 00:55:31,787
[sighs contentedly]

938
00:55:38,001 --> 00:55:40,546
Let's go drink some soju, team.

939
00:55:41,171 --> 00:55:42,172
Yes, sir.

940
00:55:43,632 --> 00:55:46,301
-We should go for a beer, too.
-Sounds great.

941
00:55:46,385 --> 00:55:48,262
I have plans, so I'll get going.

942
00:55:48,929 --> 00:55:51,306
Stay for one drink. We caught the killer.

943
00:55:51,390 --> 00:55:53,100
I'm already late. I'm off.

944
00:55:53,183 --> 00:55:54,643
-Okay, bye.
-See you tomorrow.

945
00:55:54,726 --> 00:55:55,727
Have a good evening!

946
00:55:55,811 --> 00:55:58,397
What kind of team leader
skips drinks with the team?

947
00:55:58,480 --> 00:56:00,232
Come on, bro. Let's go.

948
00:56:00,315 --> 00:56:01,692
My feelings are hurt.

949
00:56:01,775 --> 00:56:03,277
-Seriously, I'm hurt.
-[Junyoung] Let's go.

950
00:56:03,360 --> 00:56:05,070
She got a boyfriend? What's with her?

951
00:56:06,738 --> 00:56:08,156
-[Isoo] Cheers!
-[Kyungjin] Cheers!

952
00:56:11,994 --> 00:56:13,370
[exhales sharply]

953
00:56:13,453 --> 00:56:14,871
[Kyungjin and Isoo exhale sharply]

954
00:56:20,460 --> 00:56:21,670
Mmm!

955
00:56:22,087 --> 00:56:24,590
Hey, this flavor is insane.

956
00:56:24,673 --> 00:56:26,133
I've been craving this lately.

957
00:56:26,216 --> 00:56:29,344
They're famous for their gopdoritang,
but this is good too, right?

958
00:56:29,428 --> 00:56:30,721
It's so sweet and savory.

959
00:56:30,804 --> 00:56:32,431
[Junyoung] I can't stop eating it.

960
00:56:32,514 --> 00:56:34,224
I'll have to come back next time.

961
00:56:35,309 --> 00:56:37,603
With who? Your girlfriend?

962
00:56:38,895 --> 00:56:39,896
No.

963
00:56:39,980 --> 00:56:41,273
By myself.

964
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:42,983
I saw they have meals for one here.

965
00:56:43,066 --> 00:56:44,735
I'm coming back for lunch by myself.

966
00:56:45,360 --> 00:56:46,361
Mmm...

967
00:56:46,445 --> 00:56:48,071
[♪ jaunty music playing]

968
00:56:48,155 --> 00:56:49,281
[sighs deeply]

969
00:56:49,364 --> 00:56:51,617
This case was driven by
an all-consuming love.

970
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:53,910
Love is all-consuming by nature.

971
00:56:53,994 --> 00:56:55,162
Is it?

972
00:56:55,912 --> 00:56:56,997
Is it, Junyoung?

973
00:56:58,373 --> 00:57:01,209
[sighs] I've never had
an office romance before.

974
00:57:01,293 --> 00:57:03,337
It's fun to secretly date
a coworker, right?

975
00:57:04,546 --> 00:57:06,965
How does it feel? Tell me, I'm curious.

976
00:57:08,342 --> 00:57:09,384
That's enough.

977
00:57:09,468 --> 00:57:10,844
I don't know who it is.

978
00:57:10,927 --> 00:57:13,263
I just had a feeling
you were dating a coworker.

979
00:57:13,347 --> 00:57:15,849
Yeah, who could it be? I'm dying to know.

980
00:57:17,059 --> 00:57:18,101
Ah!

981
00:57:18,185 --> 00:57:20,896
No wonder he always
volunteered to go to the morgue.

982
00:57:20,979 --> 00:57:22,814
I noticed a long time ago.

983
00:57:22,898 --> 00:57:25,108
I've been dating since I was
in seventh grade.

984
00:57:25,192 --> 00:57:26,318
I'm a dating expert.

985
00:57:27,235 --> 00:57:28,570
Will you two just shut up?

986
00:57:28,654 --> 00:57:30,697
I don't think so. I'm going to say more.

987
00:57:30,781 --> 00:57:32,783
You should be keeping things professional.

988
00:57:32,866 --> 00:57:34,368
The autopsy room? How dare you!

989
00:57:34,451 --> 00:57:36,078
The autopsy room, what?

990
00:57:37,037 --> 00:57:39,414
-It's where your love blossomed.
-The autopsy room!

991
00:57:41,333 --> 00:57:43,251
[Dr. Yoon] You guys are awful.

992
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:45,087
[Junyoung] Jiwon.

993
00:57:45,754 --> 00:57:48,048
Yes, we're dating.

994
00:57:48,131 --> 00:57:50,258
Is that really something
to tease him about?

995
00:57:51,510 --> 00:57:52,844
-What's with you two?
-No.

996
00:57:53,637 --> 00:57:55,514
We should celebrate. Right, Kyungjin?

997
00:57:55,597 --> 00:57:56,598
Yes, of course.

998
00:57:56,682 --> 00:57:57,766
Right.

999
00:57:59,309 --> 00:58:01,186
[Isoo] Here, let me pour you one.

1000
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:02,312
[Dr. Yoon clears throat]

1001
00:58:03,021 --> 00:58:05,357
I thought you were the Grim Reaper.

1002
00:58:05,440 --> 00:58:06,650
Leave my Junyoung alone.

1003
00:58:07,776 --> 00:58:09,695
You know what my job is, right?

1004
00:58:09,778 --> 00:58:12,364
-Congratulations.
-Congratulations from me, too!

1005
00:58:14,074 --> 00:58:15,158
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

1006
00:58:18,120 --> 00:58:19,162
[♪ music fades]

1007
00:58:19,246 --> 00:58:20,247
That hits the spot.

1008
00:58:21,123 --> 00:58:23,583
How did you two end up together?

1009
00:58:23,667 --> 00:58:24,751
Well, we just

1010
00:58:25,544 --> 00:58:27,838
met by chance
and ended up eating together.

1011
00:58:28,588 --> 00:58:30,465
That wasn't by chance.

1012
00:58:31,341 --> 00:58:32,342
What?

1013
00:58:32,426 --> 00:58:33,677
[♪ upbeat quirky music playing]

1014
00:58:33,760 --> 00:58:35,303
I timed it and waited for you.

1015
00:58:35,387 --> 00:58:36,555
Waited!

1016
00:58:38,223 --> 00:58:39,224
Uh...

1017
00:58:39,307 --> 00:58:40,934
Really? I had no idea.

1018
00:58:41,685 --> 00:58:43,520
-Dummy.
-[sighs wearily]

1019
00:58:43,603 --> 00:58:46,273
Even a guy that clueless has a girlfriend.

1020
00:58:46,356 --> 00:58:47,774
I know.

1021
00:58:47,858 --> 00:58:49,317
[sighs] I don't get it at all. Cheers.

1022
00:58:50,193 --> 00:58:51,194
[glasses clink]

1023
00:58:51,528 --> 00:58:53,405
Remember, I asked you where you lived.

1024
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:54,489
[Isoo gags]

1025
00:58:55,407 --> 00:58:56,408
[glasses clink]

1026
00:58:58,660 --> 00:59:00,203
-[meat sizzling]
-[exhales]

1027
00:59:01,288 --> 00:59:02,289
[exhales sharply]

1028
00:59:02,873 --> 00:59:04,499
Uh, you look well.

1029
00:59:04,583 --> 00:59:06,001
That's freelancing for you.

1030
00:59:06,084 --> 00:59:08,628
It's great not being a cop.

1031
00:59:08,712 --> 00:59:11,715
All those reports.
Just thinking about it ruins my drink.

1032
00:59:11,798 --> 00:59:12,841
[both laugh]

1033
00:59:15,177 --> 00:59:16,219
What about you?

1034
00:59:16,303 --> 00:59:18,013
What's it like being back at Gangha?

1035
00:59:18,680 --> 00:59:19,973
I like it.

1036
00:59:20,056 --> 00:59:23,310
There's a real thrill
in catching murderers one by one.

1037
00:59:23,393 --> 00:59:26,146
[sighs deeply] I kind of miss that.

1038
00:59:27,939 --> 00:59:29,149
What's Jin Isoo like?

1039
00:59:30,442 --> 00:59:31,818
Jin Isoo is

1040
00:59:32,944 --> 00:59:35,906
resourceful and quick on his feet.

1041
00:59:36,490 --> 00:59:38,325
[chuckles softly]
It's fun working with him.

1042
00:59:38,408 --> 00:59:39,409
Ah...

1043
00:59:39,493 --> 00:59:41,036
I thought you'd be missing me.

1044
00:59:41,119 --> 00:59:43,663
Uh, you're the one who decided to leave.

1045
00:59:43,747 --> 00:59:45,665
-[chuckles]
-Here.

1046
00:59:51,087 --> 00:59:52,297
-Cheers.
-[glasses clink]

1047
00:59:56,468 --> 00:59:57,511
[sighs softly]

1048
01:00:00,096 --> 01:00:01,556
He's coming back in two days.

1049
01:00:02,140 --> 01:00:04,100
[♪ tense suspenseful music playing]

1050
01:00:04,184 --> 01:00:05,519
I've got everything ready.

1051
01:00:10,315 --> 01:00:11,358
[♪ music fades]

1052
01:00:12,234 --> 01:00:14,110
Sometimes, I suddenly can't breathe.

1053
01:00:15,320 --> 01:00:17,239
For no reason at all,

1054
01:00:17,322 --> 01:00:21,743
I feel like the walls are closing in
when I'm inside places like elevators.

1055
01:00:21,827 --> 01:00:25,956
I want to hear your story first.

1056
01:00:27,374 --> 01:00:28,416
What kind of story?

1057
01:00:28,500 --> 01:00:30,836
Let's start with your parents.

1058
01:00:31,920 --> 01:00:35,549
Your brother, the one you trusted
the most, killed your parents.

1059
01:00:36,842 --> 01:00:37,968
[♪ soft, poignant music playing]

1060
01:00:38,051 --> 01:00:42,305
I'd like to hear how you feel about that.

1061
01:00:44,349 --> 01:00:46,476
Did you know that I caught a psychiatrist?

1062
01:00:47,769 --> 01:00:50,939
She hypnotized me and even killed people.

1063
01:00:51,898 --> 01:00:54,526
That's why I'm not a big fan
of psychiatrists.

1064
01:00:55,277 --> 01:00:57,362
I'd rather you just give me
the medication,

1065
01:00:57,445 --> 01:00:58,613
instead of wasting time.

1066
01:01:00,448 --> 01:01:01,533
[sighs softly]

1067
01:01:01,616 --> 01:01:04,327
You experienced
some traumatic events in the past

1068
01:01:04,411 --> 01:01:06,705
and also became
the target of bombings recently.

1069
01:01:06,788 --> 01:01:10,000
This is likely why
you are experiencing these symptoms.

1070
01:01:10,750 --> 01:01:12,919
Talking honestly about your feelings

1071
01:01:13,003 --> 01:01:16,047
and finding closure
can really help your recovery.

1072
01:01:16,131 --> 01:01:17,799
You think talking about it

1073
01:01:19,050 --> 01:01:20,677
is enough to give me closure?

1074
01:01:20,760 --> 01:01:22,470
Let's give it a try.

1075
01:01:23,054 --> 01:01:24,139
[scoffs softly]

1076
01:01:24,848 --> 01:01:26,641
I'll have to find another hospital.

1077
01:01:27,434 --> 01:01:28,894
I'll give you the medication.

1078
01:01:30,687 --> 01:01:34,316
Whenever you feel like talking,
we can talk then.

1079
01:01:55,837 --> 01:01:56,880
[♪ music fades]

1080
01:01:57,339 --> 01:01:58,340
[sighs softly]

1081
01:02:11,686 --> 01:02:12,729
[bottle clicks on table]

1082
01:02:17,233 --> 01:02:19,194
[♪ gripping suspenseful music playing]

1083
01:02:27,786 --> 01:02:29,204
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

1084
01:02:36,628 --> 01:02:38,546
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

1085
01:02:42,467 --> 01:02:44,469
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

1086
01:02:53,895 --> 01:02:57,732
YU SEONGWON, THE SCULPTOR
WHO CAPTIVATED THE EUROPEAN ART WORLD,

1087
01:02:57,816 --> 01:03:01,444
RETURNS AFTER 4 YEARS
TO HOLD A SOLO EXHIBITION IN KOREA

1088
01:03:01,528 --> 01:03:05,573
RETURN
YU SEONGWON'S SOLO EXHIBITION

1089
01:03:05,657 --> 01:03:06,658
[♪ music fades]

1090
01:03:15,500 --> 01:03:17,127
[♪ ominous music playing]

1091
01:03:41,651 --> 01:03:43,611
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

1092
01:03:53,496 --> 01:03:54,998
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1093
01:04:10,847 --> 01:04:12,057
[♪ music swells]

1094
01:04:19,731 --> 01:04:20,774
[♪ music fades]

1095
01:04:20,857 --> 01:04:21,900
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 6

1096
01:04:21,983 --> 01:04:23,943
AS THE MYSTERY DEEPENS,
YU SEONGWON EMERGES

1097
01:04:24,027 --> 01:04:25,445
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1098
01:04:45,048 --> 01:04:48,468
Special Cast.
Choi Dukmoon, Lee Suk

1099
01:04:48,551 --> 01:04:51,221
♪ Every move was never mine ♪

1100
01:04:51,304 --> 01:04:54,349
♪ I don't take the checkmate ♪

1101
01:04:54,432 --> 01:04:57,519
[vocalizing]

1102
01:04:59,604 --> 01:05:02,440
[Kyungjin] Park Jaeha's magic show!
These tickets are impossible to get.

1103
01:05:02,941 --> 01:05:04,400
-[screaming]
-[Hyera] He died in a fire mid-show.

1104
01:05:04,484 --> 01:05:06,444
The escape routine went as planned.

1105
01:05:06,528 --> 01:05:08,279
Something did feel off, though.

1106
01:05:08,363 --> 01:05:09,572
-A premonition?
-Yes.

1107
01:05:09,656 --> 01:05:11,199
This was murder, not an accident.

1108
01:05:11,282 --> 01:05:13,368
Someone poured kerosene inside the coffin.

1109
01:05:13,451 --> 01:05:14,661
[Hyera] Who made the coffin?

1110
01:05:14,744 --> 01:05:15,745
Mr. Park Jaeha?

1111
01:05:15,829 --> 01:05:17,497
-I'm Park Jaehyung.
-[man] Twins?

1112
01:05:17,580 --> 01:05:19,499
Who could do something so horrific?

1113
01:05:19,582 --> 01:05:21,000
[gasps, yelps]

1114
01:05:21,084 --> 01:05:22,085
Please don't touch.

1115
01:05:22,168 --> 01:05:23,169
[Hyera] It was three days earlier.

1116
01:05:23,253 --> 01:05:25,255
[Isoo] How are a gangster
and a magician linked?

1117
01:05:25,338 --> 01:05:26,506
Bring that bastard in.

1118
01:05:26,589 --> 01:05:28,716
-[Isoo exclaims]
-Let go. Did you kill him?

1119
01:05:28,800 --> 01:05:31,553
[suspect] If I did,
you wouldn't even find a body.

1120
01:05:31,636 --> 01:05:33,304
He knew he was going to die?

1121
01:05:33,388 --> 01:05:35,515
Betting against me takes that much.

1122
01:05:39,853 --> 01:05:40,895
[♪ music fades]

1123
01:05:49,988 --> 01:05:50,989
[Changun] Joo Hyera.

1124
01:05:59,247 --> 01:06:00,248
[sighs softly]

1125
01:06:01,666 --> 01:06:03,209
Got a lot on your mind?

1126
01:06:09,549 --> 01:06:10,925
Still chasing Yu Seongwon?

1127
01:06:11,009 --> 01:06:14,304
YU SEONGWON RETURNS AFTER 4 YEARS
TO HOLD A SOLO EXHIBITION IN KOREA

1128
01:06:14,387 --> 01:06:16,472
That's why you came back, isn't it?

1129
01:06:16,556 --> 01:06:18,141
[♪ soft, pensive music playing]

1130
01:06:18,850 --> 01:06:20,310
I get how you feel.

1131
01:06:20,393 --> 01:06:22,770
It's a case you can never forget.

1132
01:06:22,854 --> 01:06:26,107
But we already
verified Yu Seongwon's alibi.

1133
01:06:31,404 --> 01:06:33,072
You're obsessed.

1134
01:06:33,573 --> 01:06:34,616
Huh?

1135
01:06:34,699 --> 01:06:36,284
That's what ruins a detective.

1136
01:06:36,367 --> 01:06:38,119
It's not an obsession.

1137
01:06:39,245 --> 01:06:40,371
Yu Seongwon...

1138
01:06:42,040 --> 01:06:43,750
will kill again.

1139
01:06:45,001 --> 01:06:46,419
And I'm going to stop him.

1140
01:06:53,927 --> 01:06:55,929
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
